A. child localizes an element; main shifts while the local is active
child after local $a[1] = 99                     (10, 99, 30)
child after main shifted                         (99, 30)
child after its scope                            (20, 20)
main  during the child local                     (10, 99, 30)
main  after shift                                (99, 30)
main  after the child scope                      (20, 20)
main  $$r, \$a[1] taken before the shift         20

B. main localizes; the child shifts during it
child shifted during the main local              (99, 30)
main  inside, after the child shift              (99, 30)
main  after its scope                            (20, 20)

C. both threads localize the same element; the inner (main) scope ends first
child after main local and exit                  (10, 99, 30)
child after its scope                            (10, 20, 30)
main  inside its local                           (10, 7, 30)
main  after its scope                            (10, 99, 30)
main  after the child scope                      (10, 20, 30)

D. child localizes; main unshifts and pushes
child after its scope                            (0, 20, 20, 30, 40)
main  after unshift 0, push 40                   (0, 10, 99, 30, 40)

E. child localizes an absent element; main shifts
child after local $a[5] = 50                     (10, 20, 30, undef, undef, 50)
child after its scope                            (20, 30, undef, undef, 50, undef)
main  after shift                                (20, 30, undef, undef, 50)
main  exists after                               0:yes 1:yes 2:no 3:no 4:yes 5:yes

F. child localizes a shared scalar
child after its scope                            (S)
main  during the child local                     (L)
main  after the child scope                      (S)

G. child localizes a present and an absent key of a shared hash; main deletes the present one
child after its scope: k, new, exists new        (1, undef, yes)
main  during the child local: k, new             (2, 3)
main  after the child scope: k, exists new       (1, yes)
